{'symbol': 'HPE', 'date': '2019-11-17 22:30:00', 'title': 'HEWLETT PACKARD ENTERPRISE INTRODUCES KUBERNETES-BASED PLATFORM FOR BARE-METAL AND EDGE TO CLOUD DEPLOYMENTS', 'text': 'HEWLETT PACKARD ENTERPRISE ANNOUNCED THE HPE CONTAINER PLATFORM, THE INDUSTRY’S FIRST ENTERPRISE-GRADE KUBERNETES-BASED CONTAINER PLATFORM DESIGNED FOR BOTH CLOUD-NATIVE APPLICATIONS AND MONOLITHIC APPLICATIONS WITH PERSISTENT STORAGE. WITH THE HPE CONTAINER PLATFORM, ENTERPRISE CUSTOMERS CAN ACCELERATE APPLICATION DEVELOPMENT FOR NEW AND EXISTING APPS " RUNNING ON BARE-METAL OR VIRTUALIZED INFRASTRUCTURE, ON ANY PUBLIC CLOUD, AND AT THE EDGE. THE HPE CONTAINER PLATFORM IS BUILT ON PROVEN INNOVATIONS FROM HPE’S ACQUISITIONS OF BLUEDATA AND MAPR,TOGETHER WITH 100% OPEN SOURCE KUBERNETES.'}
{'symbol': 'HD', 'date': '2019-11-18 22:30:00', 'title': 'THE HOME DEPOT, INC. REAFFIRMS EARNINGS GUIDANCE FOR 2019', 'text': "THE HOME DEPOT, INC. REAFFIRMED EARNINGS GUIDANCE FOR 2019. THE COMPANY IS UPDATING FISCAL 2019 SALES GUIDANCE, AND THE COMPANY IS REAFFIRMING FISCAL 2019 EARNINGS-PER-SHARE GUIDANCE. THE COMPANY EXPECTS ITS FISCAL 2019 SALES TO GROW BY APPROXIMATELY 1.8% AND COMP SALES FOR THE COMPARABLE 52-WEEK PERIOD TO INCREASE APPROXIMATELY 3.5%. THIS COMPARES TO THE COMPANY'S PRIOR FISCAL 2019 SALES GROWTH GUIDANCE OF 2.3% AND COMP SALES GROWTH OF 4.0%. THE COMPANY REAFFIRMED ITS DILUTED EARNINGS-PER-SHARE GUIDANCE FOR THE YEAR AND EXPECTS DILUTED EARNINGS-PER-SHARE GROWTH OF APPROXIMATELY 3.1% FROM FISCAL 2018 TO $10.03."}
{'symbol': 'HPQ', 'date': '2019-11-18 22:30:00', 'title': 'HP PROVIDES INFORMATION TO SHAREHOLDERS', 'text': "ON NOVEMBER 19, 2019, HP INC. ANNOUNCED THAT IT HAS REJECTED $US33BN ($48.4BN) TAKEOVER OFFER FROM XEROX CORP AS TOO LOW, BUT IT WAS INTERESTED IN DISCUSSING A DEAL TO COMBINE WITH ITS SMALLER RIVAL. THE COMPANY STATED THAT IT RECOGNIZED THE BENEFITS OF CONSOLIDATION AND WAS ‘OPEN TO EXPLORING A POTENTIAL COMBINATION WITH XEROX’. IN ADDITION, THE COMPANY STATED IN ITS LETTER IT URGED XEROX TO LET IT PERFORM ADDITIONAL DUE DILIGENCE SO IT COULD BETTER UNDERSTAND XEROX'S RECENT REVENUE DECLINES AND ANALYZE POTENTIAL COST SAVINGS FROM A COMBINATION, WHICH XEROX HAS PEGGED AT $US2BN."}
