{'symbol': 'TRMB', 'date': '2019-11-18 22:30:00', 'title': 'TRIMBLE, HILTI AND BOSTON DYNAMICS PARTNER TO EXPLORE THE USE OF AUTONOMOUS ROBOTS IN CONSTRUCTION', 'text': 'TRIMBLE HILTI AND BOSTON DYNAMICS ANNOUNCED A COLLABORATION TO EXPLORE THE INTEGRATION OF TRIMBLE\'S AND HILTI\'S CONSTRUCTION MANAGEMENT SOFTWARE SOLUTIONS, GNSS TECHNOLOGY AND REALITY CAPTURE DEVICES WITH BOSTON DYNAMICS\' SPOT ROBOT PLATFORM. AUTONOMOUS ROBOTS CAN PLAY A SIGNIFICANT ROLE IN CONSTRUCTION, SPECIFICALLY IN PRODUCTION AND QUALITY CONTROL WORKFLOWS BY ENABLING AUTOMATION OF ROUTINE AND TEDIOUS TASKS, REDUCING WORKLOAD AND IMPROVING SAFETY. THE COMPANIES WILL COLLABORATE TO DEVELOP A "PROOF-OF-CONCEPT" SOLUTION. EQUIPPED WITH TRIMBLE\'S AND HILTI\'S REALITY CAPTURE DEVICES AS ITS PAYLOAD AND DIRECTLY COMMUNICATING WITH A CLOUD-BASED CONSTRUCTION MANAGEMENT APPLICATION, THE BOSTON DYNAMICS SPOT ROBOT WILL BE ABLE TO PROVIDE CONSISTENT OUTPUT, DELIVER IMPROVED EFFICIENCY ON REPEATABLE TASKS AND ENABLE UP-TO-DATE AS-BUILT DATA ANALYSIS. THE AUTONOMOUS, TERRAIN-AGNOSTIC CAPABILITIES SUPPORT THE DYNAMIC NATURE OF THE CONSTRUCTION ENVIRONMENT, ENABLING THE ROBOT TO BY-PASS OBSTACLES AND MAINTAIN ITS DEFINED PATH TO SUPPORT ROUTINE TASKS SUCH AS DAILY SITE SCANS, PROGRESS MONITORING, ASSET MANAGEMENT AND REMOTE SUPPORT. MULTI-DIRECTIONAL COMMUNICATION BETWEEN THE ROBOT, TRIMBLE\'S AND HILTI\'S PAYLOADS AND THE CLOUD APPLICATION SUPPORT A CONTINUOUS FLOW OF INFORMATION AND CLOSES THE LOOP FOR THE CONSTRUCTION ENVIRONMENT.'}
{'symbol': 'TRMB', 'date': '2019-11-18 09:30:00', 'title': 'TRIMBLE APPOINTS DAVID BARNES AS CFO', 'text': 'TRIMBLE ANNOUNCES NEW CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER.TRIMBLE INC - DAVID BARNES WILL BE JOINING TRIMBLE ON DECEMBER 2, 2019 AND WILL SERVE AS ITS CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER (CFO) EFFECTIVE JANUARY 4, 2020.TRIMBLE INC - BARNES SERVED AS CFO AT MWH GLOBAL INC.'}
{'symbol': 'TRMB', 'date': '2019-11-17 22:30:00', 'title': 'DAVID G. BARNES TO SERVE AS CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER OF TRIMBLE INC., EFFECTIVE JANUARY 4, 2020', 'text': 'TRIMBLE INC. ANNOUNCED THAT DAVID G. BARNES WILL BE JOINING THE COMPANY ON DECEMBER 2, 2019 AND WILL SERVE AS ITS CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER (CFO) EFFECTIVE JANUARY 4, 2020. BARNES SERVED AS CFO AT MWH GLOBAL INC. BARNES HAS MORE THAN 35 YEARS OF FINANCIAL AND STRATEGIC MANAGEMENT EXPERIENCE. AT MWH, BARNES SERVED ON THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS AND HAD RESPONSIBILITY FOR INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY AND PROCUREMENT IN ADDITION TO HIS FINANCIAL ROLE. PRIOR TO BEING CFO AT MWH, BARNES HELD FINANCIAL LEADERSHIP POSITIONS AT WESTERN UNION, COORS, AND YUM BRANDS.'}
{'symbol': 'TYL', 'date': '2019-11-18 22:30:00', 'title': 'TWO MORE CALIFORNIA SUPERIOR COURTS SELECT TYLER TECHNOLOGIES’ ODYSSEY CASE MANAGEMENT SOLUTION', 'text': 'TYLER TECHNOLOGIES, INC. ANNOUNCED THAT IT HAS SIGNED AGREEMENTS WITH THE SUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF MENDOCINO, AND THE SUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF SHASTA, FOR TYLER’S ODYSSEY® CASE MANAGEMENT SOLUTION. THESE AGREEMENTS REPRESENT THE 27TH AND 28TH CALIFORNIA SUPERIOR COURTS TO SELECT TYLER’S ODYSSEY SOLUTION, WHICH NOW SERVES APPROXIMATELY 70% OF CALIFORNIA’S POPULATION. THROUGH A NEW MASTER SERVICES AGREEMENT (MSA) WITH THE STATE OF CALIFORNIA, TYLER IS NOW A PREFERRED CASE MANAGEMENT VENDOR, MAKING THE PROCESS FOR COURTS TO PROCURE ODYSSEY QUICK AND EASY. THE COUNTY OF MENDOCINO IS IN NORTHERN CALIFORNIA, EQUIDISTANT FROM THE SAN FRANCISCO BAY AREA AND THE CALIFORNIA/OREGON BORDER. THE MENDOCINO SUPERIOR COURT CHOSE TYLER’S ODYSSEY CASE MANAGEMENT, JUDGE EDITION, AND CLERK EDITION SOLUTIONS TO REPLACE ITS CURRENT CASE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM, WHICH LACKS E-FILING AND OTHER MODERN FUNCTIONALITY. THE SUPERIOR COURT WAS LOOKING TO REPLACE ITS CURRENT CASE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM THAT WOULD NO LONGER BE SUPPORTED BY ITS CURRENT PROVIDER AND SELECTED TYLER’S ODYSSEY SOLUTION TO MANAGE ALL CASE TYPES, ALONG WITH ODYSSEY JUDGE EDITION™ AND ODYSSEY CLERK EDITION™. LIKE MENDOCINO, SHASTA WILL ALSO UTILIZE ODYSSEY JUDGE EDITION AND ODYSSEY CLERK EDITION.'}
{'symbol': 'TSN', 'date': '2019-11-18 10:30:00', 'title': 'TYSON BEEF PLANT IN KANSAS TO RESUME OPERATIONS IN DECEMBER', 'text': "TYSON BEEF PLANT IN KANSAS TO RESUME OPERATIONS IN DECEMBER.TYSON FOODS - TYSON FRESH MEATS PLANS TO RESUME RECEIVING CATTLE AT HOLCOMB FACILITY FIRST WEEK OF DECEMBER.TYSON FOODS - POST AUG 9 FIRE DISRUPTED OPERATIONS AT HOLCOMB, KANSAS BEEF COMPLEX, UNIT SAYS RECONSTRUCTION OF FACILITY IS NEAR COMPLETION.TYSON FOODS - EFFORTS TO RESUME HARVEST OPERATIONS WILL BEGIN FIRST WEEK OF DECEMBER, WITH INTENTIONS TO BE FULLY OPERATIONAL BY FIRST WEEK OF JANUARY.TYSON FOODS - SINCE FIRE, CATTLE HAVE BEEN DIVERTED TO CO'S OTHER BEEF FACILITIES, WHERE THEY WERE ABLE TO OFFSET SOME OF PRODUCTION VOLUME LOSSES."}
